  "note": "Borough election of ten councillors, poll due 18 May 1949; only seven nominations were received for the ten seats, so there was no contest (Irish News, 6 May 1949, p. 3). 'In Larne only seven nominations were received for ten vacancies. Messrs. J. A. Gray, W. H. Esler and J. L. Hogg did not go forward. The retiring members nominated in the other wards are—' followed by the seven names above. Returned unopposed."
